---@class posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlert
---@field id string Unique identifier of this alert instance.
---@field grouping_key string Key of the result group this instance tracks. Empty when the source does not group results.
---@field state posthog.platform_alerts.BillingAlertConfigurationStateEnum Current state of this alert instance. * `not_firing` - Not firing * `firing` - Firing * `errored` - Errored * `snoozed` - Snoozed * `broken` - Broken
---@field firing_started_at string|distilled.Null When the current firing started. Null when the instance is not firing.
---@field last_notified_at string|distilled.Null When a notification was last sent for this instance.
---@field snooze_until string|distilled.Null Time until which notifications are snoozed. Null when not snoozed.
---@field labels posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertLabelsMap Result labels and their values for the group this instance tracks, such as {"service_name": "checkout"}. Empty when the source does not group results.

---* `ok` - OK
---* `errored` - Errored
---* `broken` - Broken
---@alias posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertCheckStatusEnum "ok"|"errored"|"broken"

---@class posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfiguration
---@field id string Unique identifier of the alert configuration.
---@field name string Human-readable name of the alert.
---@field enabled boolean Whether the alert is evaluated on schedule.
---@field source_kind posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfigurationSourceKindEnum Product whose data the alert evaluates. * `logs` - Logs * `insight` - Insight * `warehouse_source` - Warehouse source * `warehouse_destination` - Warehouse destination * `metrics` - Metrics
---@field source_config posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfigurationSourceConfigMap Source-specific settings. The shape depends on source_kind. The bound the alert is evaluated against is under the condition key.
---@field check_interval_minutes number Minutes between scheduled checks. Applies when recurrence_unit is null.
---@field recurrence_unit posthog.platform_alerts.CalendarUnitEnum|distilled.Null Calendar unit the alert recurs on. Null means it recurs on check_interval_minutes. * `day` - Day * `week` - Week * `month` - Month
---@field anchor_time string|distilled.Null Local time (HH:MM in the project timezone) a calendar recurrence lands on. Null means the default anchor for the unit.
---@field evaluation_periods number Number of recent checks considered when deciding to fire.
---@field datapoints_to_alarm number Number of breaching checks within evaluation_periods required to fire.
---@field cooldown_minutes number Minimum minutes between notifications for the same alert.
---@field schedule_restriction posthog.platform_alerts.AlertScheduleRestriction|distilled.Null Blocked local time windows (HH:MM in the project timezone) when the alert does not run. Null means no quiet hours.
---@field next_check_at string|distilled.Null When the next check is due. Null when no check is scheduled.
---@field consecutive_failures number Number of checks in a row that failed to evaluate.
---@field legacy_configuration_id string|distilled.Null ID of the legacy source configuration this row was backfilled from. Null for alerts created on the platform.
---@field grouping posthog.platform_alerts.Grouping How the alert splits its results into instances.
---@field snooze_until string|distilled.Null Time until which every instance's notifications are muted. Null when not muted. An instance's own snooze_until mutes one group, and the later of the two holds.
---@field check_status posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertCheckStatusEnum Whether the alert's checks succeed. Holds for every instance, because a failed check names no group. * `ok` - OK * `errored` - Errored * `broken` - Broken
---@field overflowed_groups number New groups the last successful check could not track because the alert already held grouping.max_instances instances. 0 when every group fit.
---@field overflow_is_lower_bound boolean Whether the last successful check cut its results before counting overflowed_groups. When true, more groups than overflowed_groups may be untracked.
---@field owner posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertOwnerEnum Which stack evaluates and delivers the alert. Only an alert the platform owns can be edited here. The source product's own API edits the rest. * `source` - Source * `platform` - Platform
---@field created_at string When the configuration was created.
---@field updated_at string When the configuration was last changed.
---@field alerts posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfigurationAlertsList Runtime state for each result group of this configuration.
---@field labels posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfigurationLabelsMap Labels that say who owns the alert and how urgent it is, such as {"team": "checkout", "severity": "critical"}. Names use letters, digits and underscores. alertname and names that start with posthog_ are reserved. Values cannot use templates.
---@field annotations posthog.platform_alerts.PlatformAlertConfigurationAnnotationsMap Context for whoever responds, such as {"runbook_url": "https://..."}. Values can use {{ $labels.<name> }} for a grouping key or label of the alert, and {{ $value }}. An annotation whose name ends in _url must start with https://.

