---The settings of a new alert. Every one but source_config has a default, which is stored.
---@class posthog.platform_alerts.WarehouseDestinationPlatformAlertConfigurationCreate
---@field source_kind string Product whose data the alert evaluates. It cannot change after the create.
---@field name? string Human-readable name of the alert. Defaults to 'Untitled alert'.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the alert is evaluated on schedule. Defaults to true.
---@field source_config posthog.platform_alerts.WarehouseDestinationAlertConfig Settings for a warehouse_destination alert. The bound the alert is evaluated against is under condition.
---@field grouping? posthog.platform_alerts.Grouping How the alert splits its results into instances. Defaults to mode single.
---@field schedule_restriction? posthog.platform_alerts.AlertScheduleRestriction|distilled.Null Blocked local time windows (HH:MM in the project timezone) when the alert does not notify. Null means no quiet hours. Defaults to null.
---@field evaluation_periods? number Number of recent checks considered when deciding to fire. Defaults to 1.
---@field datapoints_to_alarm? number Number of breaching checks within evaluation_periods required to fire. Cannot exceed evaluation_periods. Defaults to 1.
---@field cooldown_minutes? number Minimum minutes between notifications for the same alert. Defaults to 0.
---@field labels? posthog.platform_alerts.WarehouseDestinationPlatformAlertConfigurationCreateLabelsMap Labels that say who owns the alert and how urgent it is, such as {"team": "checkout", "severity": "critical"}. Names use letters, digits and underscores. alertname and names that start with posthog_ are reserved. Values cannot use templates.
---@field annotations? posthog.platform_alerts.WarehouseDestinationPlatformAlertConfigurationCreateAnnotationsMap Context for whoever responds, such as {"runbook_url": "https://..."}. Values can use {{ $labels.<name> }} for a grouping key or label of the alert, and {{ $value }}. An annotation whose name ends in _url must start with https://.

---Context for whoever responds, such as {"runbook_url": "https://..."}. Values can use {{ $labels.<name> }} for a grouping key or label of the alert, and {{ $value }}. An annotation whose name ends in _url must start with https://.
